5 #edb/ref 17592186443996 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444005 1075 #edb/ref 17592186443997 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444005 1075 #edb/ref 17592186443998 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444005 1075 #edb/ref 17592186443999 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444005 1075 #edb/ref 17592186444000 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444005 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444005 1077 "selection" 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444005 1078 #edb/ref 17592186444000 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444005 1079 #uuid "47117b4f-de1f-5179-8ffa-cfd17b335562" 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444006 1075 #edb/ref 17592186443995 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444006 1075 #edb/ref 17592186444001 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444006 1075 #edb/ref 17592186444002 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444006 1075 #edb/ref 17592186444003 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444006 1075 #edb/ref 17592186444004 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444006 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444006 1077 "selection" 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444006 1078 #edb/ref 17592186444003 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444006 1079 #uuid "585f5d02-4d6c-51a6-9fd9-0f3602ee74e4" 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444007 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444005 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444007 1069 "q-64796" 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444007 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444007 1071 "Given the equation ${y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{′}+\\frac{1}{16}y=0$ for $y=y(x),$ which of the following is **not** a solution to this equation?" 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444007 1072 #uuid "5dbc9673-510f-532c-a004-54ed22aabfa7" 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444007 1074 "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+\\frac{1}{2}\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+\\frac{1}{16}{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\lambda +\\frac{1}{16}) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\lambda +\\frac{1}{16} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\lambda +\\frac{1}{4})}^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand so $\\lambda =-\\frac{1}{4}$ is a repeated root of the auxiliary equation.\n\nTherefore, any linear combination of the functions ${e}^{-x/4}$ and $x{e}^{-x/4}$ is a solution to the original differential equation. \n\nAmong the given options, only $2{e}^{-4x}+3x{e}^{-x/4}$ is not a solution." 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444008 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444006 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444008 1069 "q-64795" 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444008 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444008 1071 "Given the equation ${y}^{″}-18{y}^{′}+81y=0$ for $y=y(t),$ which of the following is **not** a solution to this equation?" 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444008 1072 #uuid "5e9b8a76-fadd-5c5e-88d1-453c1509beac" 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444008 1074 "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda t}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda t},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda t}-18\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda t}+81{e}^{\\lambda t} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda t}({\\lambda }^{2}-18\\lambda +81) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-18\\lambda +81 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda -9)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand so $\\lambda =9$ is a repeated root of the auxiliary equation.\n\nTherefore, any linear combination of the functions ${e}^{9t}$ and $t{e}^{9t}$ is a solution to the original differential equation. \n\nAmong the given options, only $3{e}^{-9t}$ is not a solution." 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444009 1058 #edb/ref 17592186444013 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444009 1062 #uuid "0f286fd7-1908-5288-96d6-dcf89110d360" 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444009 1063 #edb/ref 17592186348053 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444010 1058 #edb/ref 17592186444011 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444010 1062 #uuid "12f24fc0-6891-5b1a-9924-a75b1a7ee50c" 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444010 1063 #edb/ref 17592186265839 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444011 1062 #uuid "3d0273da-7dca-5b4d-9e87-7ca443d6f6e9" 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444011 1063 #edb/ref 17592186265843 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444012 1058 #edb/ref 17592186444010 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444012 1062 #uuid "4a132e70-8467-55e5-b1db-1bc17136f384" 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444012 1063 #edb/ref 17592186444007 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444013 1058 #edb/ref 17592186444012 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444013 1062 #uuid "6a42458d-290e-54dd-b688-d7fd5bd9fa4a" 13194139534914 17592186045417 true] [17592186444013 1063 #edb/ref 17592186444008 13194139534914 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-d70c6a0e-1f3c-563a-8c55-406c4c3e138f" 17592186443994 "answer-05281020-031d-5d2a-808e-01688d4b6930" 17592186443995 "answer-19665675-933f-562b-92c2-453f3aa6a7c3" 17592186443996 "answe